/-!
# Primitive endpoint and bin witnesses for the last-cell Gamma moments

The expensive original full-grid computation is no longer evaluated in
any closed numerical theorem. The 13 exponential intervals are exact
audit-scale values, checked for equality to the existing certified
generator. Only the needed lower contributions at A and upper
contributions at B are evaluated, with one independent check per w-bin.
Their outward 10^-16 endpoint sums fit the original 10^-8 moment table.
All analytic containment is transferred from existing full-moment
soundness; the external data have no trusted numerical status.
-/

namespace W5

def thetaLastCellWExpBox (l u : ℤ) : QInterval :=
  ⟨(l:ℚ)/(thetaAuditScale:ℚ), (u:ℚ)/(thetaAuditScale:ℚ)⟩

